+/// The GPU times of the passes that one command buffer encodes after its first timestamp write. Each pass samples the
+/// GPU timestamp at its start and its end, the stage boundaries at which Apple GPUs sample counters. A timestamp written
+/// between passes reads the latest end of the passes before it, or, before the first pass, the start of the first
+/// pass after it, as Vulkan's bottom-of-pipe timestamps do.
+class API_AVAILABLE(macos(11.0), ios(14.0), tvos(14.0), visionos(2.0)) MDPassTimeline {
+	/// Per sample, in nanoseconds; 0 for a sample that the GPU did not take, such as one of an empty pass.
